            <div xml:id="d754">

                <pb facs="0587" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2001.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mexican
                        Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 54.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to your note of the 19th
                    ultimo, communicating to the Department a request of your Government that
                    measures be taken to prevent the enlistment of men in the United States for the
                    invasion of Lower California, I have the honor to inform you that I am advised
                    by the Attorney General, under date of the 30th ultimo, that this matter is
                    already in the hands of the United States attorney at José Angeles, to whom he
                    has forwarded a copy of your note, with instructions to proceed appropriately in
                    the premises.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
